{"id": "EUVD-2026-69287", "enisaUuid": "8ec5f862-688c-3778-a2ff-27cea06df35d", "description": "A flaw was found in the SFTP backend in gvfs. When mounting a share and reading a file, a malicious SFTP server can cause read_reply() to process a length that exceeds the size requested by the client. The function does not verify the server-provided length against the allocated buffer size, causing the operation to write past the intended boundaries. This issue allows a malicious server to corrupt adjacent heap memory in the gvfsd-sftp process, resulting in a denial of service as the process aborts upon detecting the heap corruption or potentially allowing arbitrary code execution.", "datePublished": "2026-09-01T15:15:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T05:23:39", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:73997", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:73998", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:74370", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:85939", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:85940", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:85941", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:85942", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:85943", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:85944", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:85945", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:86606", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-84268", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2526485", "https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gvfs/-/issues/862"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-84268", "GHSA-8cxg-v7p7-qc7j"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.46, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0df0fe7a-b5a9-3751-9709-935a8ed56b7c", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9.2 Update Services for SAP Solutions", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:1.48.1-4.el9_2.1"}, {"id": "1268090a-90d0-375c-adf3-ff67fc24fbb4", "